there's a wacky and ridiculous headline  that appeared on screen on fox news  that's obviously really dumb but it's  actually also a serious thing that I  want to talk about which with you which  is the total misunderstanding of Latin  America that exists these lower-third  images matter that show up at the bottom  when you tune in to MSNBC or CNN or Fox  News even before you listen to what's  being said to figure out what the topic  is to see if you're interested you often  will just read what's at the bottom of  the screen the lower third as it's often  called um and when Donald Trump over the  weekend announced that he was going to  be cutting aid to three Latin American  countries El Salvador Guatemala and  Honduras these are three countries right  this is not Mexico these are three other  countries FoxNews erroneously  inadvertently wrote the headline that  Donald Trump cuts aid to three Mexican  countries that's what it said on screen  Trump cuts US aid to three Mexican  countries so yes hahaha they don't know  geography they don't know about Latin  America these are countries that many  people come to the u.s. from so they are  Mexico through Mexico so they are  Mexican countries fine it's nonsense and  Fox News apologized for it and then they  corrected it but there's actually a  really deep thing that I want to talk  about and this is the perfect  opportunity to talk about it and there's  a sort of geopolitical side and then  there's a personal side which I'll tell  you about this  so first the geopolitical lots of  Americans don't know about all of these  Latin American countries when they think  about immigration they sort of imagine  people from this mess of countries below  Mexico it's people who are basically  just like Mexicans they speak Spanish  who most importantly are trying to  invade the United States through the  southern border so it doesn't really  matter if they're coming from Guatemala  or Honduras or Costa Rica Panama or  Venezuela or wherever and of course  they're only coming from some of these  countries in any significant numbers in  the same way that they don't care to  know or understand the differences  between like single-payer versus  medicare-for-all versus a nationalized  healthcare system it's just it's  communism in the minds of many people  they don't care or know the differences  between what's happening in Mexico  versus what's happening in Honduras  versus Guatemala or the fact that these  countries have different indigenous  groups each of whom have different  cultures and different histories and  very often speak different languages in  addition to Spanish and they definitely  have no idea that the United States  relationships to these countries in the  last hundred years has been drastically  different if you consider the US history  in Nicaragua for example to the US  history with Costa Rica and Mexico as an  example there is very little in common  other than yeah a bunch of the people in  these countries speak Spanish so in a  sense the stupid-head line of Trump is  cutting aid to three Mexican countries  it's more accurate than you can imagine  in terms of the worldview that exists  for many of these right-wingers and  Trump Asst so that's on the geopolitical  side now on the personal individual sort  of identity politics I'd even relatively  educated people are very confused about  Latin America I have this funny anecdote  where someone I know has family has  cousins who live in a rural conservative  part of the United States and there was  a point in time where where the the the  cousins were sort of confused they've  somehow heard I David speaks Spanish oh  I speak Spanish yeah David speak Spanish  he's from Argentina and they said oh  he's Mexican wait wait he speaks Spanish  he's Mexican no he's from Argentina  that's a different country it's in South  America not in Central America lots of  countries speak Spanish Mexican is a  nationality oh but isn't David's white  right yet that's right he is white and  his ethnicity is you know Ashkenazi  Jewish but you can be from any country  and speak any language and then it was  wait there are Jews in Mexico and the  answer is of course there are Jews in  Mexico but David's not from Mexico Dave  is from Argentina so the stupid headline  is sadly I wish it weren't the case I  wish we could just laugh it off as some  dumb thing on Fox News it actually is a  really good opportunity to point out  there are a lot of understandings out  there about Latin America and in the  same way that many people in the West  see that jumble of countries when you  look at a map of Africa as not  particularly distinct and only when you  actually inform yourself do you realize  about countries that where French is  spoken that are very distinct from other  parts of Africa northern and southern  Africa West Africa and all of these  different conflicts and and sort of  internal politics there's a very similar  sort of perspective with Latin and South  America and it doesn't make any sense  and this stupid headline on Fox News as  dumb as it is actually is sort of  opening the door to a lot of that so I'm  kind of glad to have the opportunity to  discuss it because I don't know how else  I would kind of randomly bring it up but  anyway Fox News they apologized and who  knows who they blamed it doesn't even  matter at this point some kind of error  in the control room as they often say  but that is actually the perspective of  many people when they hear that these  three countries are no longer getting  aid from the United States what they  imagine is these are all countries where  people just come in over the us-mexico  border  let's cut aid to all of them until they  do what we want and what that is never  exactly clear when you hear Trump say  they're not even doing anything for us  make sure you're following the show on  Instagram at David Pakman show we will  take a quick break next I will be joined  by David F